data.reasoningText:
The source generator still can't generate for ResponseError because of SYSLIB1220 (the internal converter blocks it) and SYSLIB1030 (didn't generate metadata). Even with the custom converter specified via `[JsonSourceGenerationOptions]`, the source generator is blocked by the type's own `[JsonConverter]` attribute pointing to an inaccessible converter.

I need to abandon the source-gen context approach for ResponseError and instead use the converter directly. Let me just call the custom converter methods directly instead of going through JsonSerializer:

```csharp
// Serialize:
new ResponseErrorAotConverter().Write(writer, Error, null);


// Deserialize:
ResponseErrorAotConverter.Read(property.Value);
```

This bypasses JsonSerializer entirely and is fully AOT-safe.

